From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:38:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Sentinel integrity seam on the client intent packets

One static call per handler into dev.btc.core.integrity.SentinelHooks, and
nothing else: movement, attack, entity interaction, item use (in the air and
on a block) and container clicks. The seam is uninstalled by default, so an
unarmed server pays a volatile read and a null check on its hottest path.

The call sits immediately after ensureRunningOnSameThread, before any of the
handler's own guards, so the engine sees what the client claimed rather than
what the server was willing to accept.

Server-side teleports are framed rather than inferred: the expectation is
announced where awaitingPositionFromClient is armed, and closed where the
client acknowledges it. Between the two, the positions the client keeps
sending are about the place it has not left yet. The teleport cause is
deliberately absent here, since PlayerTeleportEvent already carries it to
ordinary listener code.

